WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.057
The Emperor's New Clothes

00:00:02.757 --> 00:00:11.653
Many years ago, in a bustling kingdom across the sea, lived an Emperor who cared more about new clothes than anything else in the whole wide world!

00:00:12.003 --> 00:00:22.627
While other rulers spent their mornings reviewing maps, inspecting castles, or meeting with ministers, the people of this city always said: The Emperor is in his wardrobe!

00:00:22.977 --> 00:00:26.625
He had a different splendid coat for every single hour of the day.

00:00:27.275 --> 00:00:31.777
One bright morning, two sneaky strangers came walking into the royal capital.

00:00:32.127 --> 00:00:37.737
They bowed low before the guards and announced themselves as master weavers from a distant land.

00:00:38.087 --> 00:00:48.711
They claimed they could weave the most extraordinary fabric ever known, cloth so magical that it was completely invisible to anyone who was foolish or unfit for their job!

00:00:49.361 --> 00:00:52.732
When the Emperor heard the news, his eyes danced with joy.

00:00:53.082 --> 00:00:55.109
What a magnificent suit that would be!

00:00:55.459 --> 00:00:56.547
he exclaimed.

00:00:56.897 --> 00:01:03.382
If I wore such clothes, I could discover at once which men in my kingdom are wise and which are simpletons!

00:01:03.732 --> 00:01:11.476
Without delay, he gave the two weavers a great chest overflowing with shiny gold coins so they could start weaving immediately.

00:01:12.126 --> 00:01:16.777
The two rogues promptly set up two large wooden looms in a grand palace hall.

00:01:17.127 --> 00:01:21.031
They demanded the finest silk thread and pure spools of spun gold.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:26.351
But as soon as the treasures were brought, they stuffed them straight into their own traveling knapsacks!

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:33.464
Then, sitting at the empty frames, they pumped the pedals and clicked their empty shuttles through the air late into the night.

00:01:34.114 --> 00:01:39.661
After a few days, the Emperor grew impatient to see how his wonderful cloth was turning out.

00:01:40.011 --> 00:01:43.360
I will send my faithful old minister, thought the Emperor.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.870
He is sensible and wise, and nobody is better suited for his post.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:52.508
The old minister adjusted his spectacles and stepped into the weaving hall.

00:01:52.858 --> 00:01:56.015
But when he looked at the looms, he stopped dead in his tracks!

00:01:56.665 --> 00:02:01.913
The minister rubbed his spectacles and stared again, but there was not a single thread to be seen!

00:02:02.263 --> 00:02:03.351
Mercy on me!

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.131
thought the poor old man.

00:02:05.481 --> 00:02:07.038
Can it be that I am foolish?

00:02:07.388 --> 00:02:08.903
No one must ever know!

00:02:09.253 --> 00:02:15.055
The weavers smiled warmly and asked: Do you not admire these rich scarlet swirls, Sir Minister?

00:02:15.405 --> 00:02:16.728
Oh, magnificent!

00:02:17.078 --> 00:02:18.657
gasped the minister aloud.

00:02:19.007 --> 00:02:20.308
Exquisite colors!

00:02:20.658 --> 00:02:22.429
I shall tell the Emperor at once!

00:02:23.079 --> 00:02:28.540
Next, the Emperor sent his trusted Royal Chamberlain to find out when the suit would be finished.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:32.879
The Chamberlain leaned over the wooden frame, squinting left and right.

00:02:33.229 --> 00:02:37.155
Just like the minister, he saw nothing but bare wood and empty air!

00:02:37.505 --> 00:02:39.723
Can I be unfit for my grand office?

00:02:40.073 --> 00:02:40.991
he worried.

00:02:41.341 --> 00:02:44.007
So he bowed gracefully and cried: Charming!

00:02:44.357 --> 00:02:46.320
A masterpiece of silk and gold!

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.594
Now the entire city could talk of nothing else!

00:02:49.944 --> 00:02:53.784
At last, the Emperor decided to see the magical cloth for himself.

00:02:54.134 --> 00:02:57.931
Flanked by his finest courtiers, he swept into the weaving room.

00:02:58.281 --> 00:03:02.463
The weavers worked faster than ever, slicing the air with clicking scissors.

00:03:02.813 --> 00:03:06.226
The Emperor blinked once, blinked twice, and rubbed his eyes.

00:03:06.576 --> 00:03:08.475
He could not see a single strand!

00:03:09.125 --> 00:03:10.255
This is terrible!

00:03:10.605 --> 00:03:11.779
thought the Emperor.

00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:13.238
Am I foolish?

00:03:13.588 --> 00:03:15.316
Am I unfit to be Emperor?

00:03:15.666 --> 00:03:18.375
But on no account would he let anyone suspect!

00:03:18.725 --> 00:03:21.136
Oh, it has my highest royal approval!

00:03:21.486 --> 00:03:23.406
he declared with a beaming smile.

00:03:23.756 --> 00:03:28.471
The night before the great city procession, the weavers lit sixteen bright candles.

00:03:28.821 --> 00:03:33.791
Everyone could see them busily cutting the empty air and sewing with threadless needles.

00:03:34.441 --> 00:03:38.921
At dawn, the rogues raised their arms as if holding up a delicate garment.

00:03:39.271 --> 00:03:41.127
Here are your Majesty's trousers!

00:03:41.477 --> 00:03:42.949
Here is the waistcoat!

00:03:43.299 --> 00:03:45.155
And here is the royal mantle!

00:03:45.505 --> 00:03:51.820
The fabric is as light as a cobweb, you might think you have nothing on at all, but that is its greatest virtue!

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:56.991
The Emperor removed his robes and prepared to try on his extraordinary new suit.

00:03:57.641 --> 00:04:04.959
The rogues pretended to fasten invisible buttons, smooth invisible sleeves, and drape a splendid invisible train.

00:04:05.309 --> 00:04:12.519
The Emperor twirled around slowly before a tall golden mirror, standing in his ruffled bedtime drawers and undershirt.

00:04:12.869 --> 00:04:14.512
How delightfully they fit!

00:04:14.862 --> 00:04:16.057
purred the courtiers.

00:04:16.407 --> 00:04:17.900
What a glorious pattern!

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.509
What royal colors!

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.676
The royal canopy is ready, your Majesty!

00:04:23.026 --> 00:04:24.989
announced the master of ceremonies.

00:04:25.339 --> 00:04:34.747
The noble lords of the bedchamber knelt down upon the velvet carpet and reached out with both hands, pretending to lift the magnificent invisible train.

00:04:35.097 --> 00:04:41.731
They marched forward with their arms held high in the air, terrified that someone might think them foolish if they let go!

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:47.864
Under a high silk canopy embroidered with gold, the Emperor strode through the sunlit capital.

00:04:48.214 --> 00:04:55.041
The cobblestone avenue was lined with cheering crowds, and spectators leaned out of every flower-decked window.

00:04:55.391 --> 00:04:57.396
Look at his Majesty's new clothes!

00:04:57.746 --> 00:04:59.410
people cried to one another.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.168
What a graceful train!

00:05:01.518 --> 00:05:02.819
What a perfect fit!

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:06.007
No one dared admit they could see nothing at all.

00:05:06.657 --> 00:05:14.422
Just as the procession entered the bustling town square, a little boy perched upon his father's shoulders pointed with a bright giggle.

00:05:14.772 --> 00:05:15.817
Look, Papa!

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:20.157
cried the child in a clear, happy voice that echoed across the stones.

00:05:20.507 --> 00:05:22.619
The Emperor has no clothes on at all!

00:05:22.969 --> 00:05:29.475
The father gasped, and the words whispered like a wave from neighbor to neighbor: The child says he has nothing on!

00:05:30.125 --> 00:05:31.683
He has nothing on at all!

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:35.489
shouted all the people in a great chorus of friendly laughter.

00:05:35.839 --> 00:05:39.743
The Emperor shivered, and his cheeks turned red as a ripe strawberry.

00:05:40.093 --> 00:05:42.418
He knew deep down that the people were right!

00:05:42.768 --> 00:05:52.240
But he squared his shoulders, lifted his golden crown, and marched even taller, learning that true dignity comes from honesty, not from fancy clothes.

